  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Category dropdown options are fixed to the three the idea names (Novel, Cookbook, Reference); no custom categories are added since the idea specifies a dropdown of those three.",
    "Persistence uses browser localStorage behind a repository boundary so storage can be swapped without touching the UI; no backend is needed for a single-user family tracker.",
    "Borrower name is collected inline when 'Lend out' is pressed rather than via a separate modal, and lending with an empty borrower name is ignored.",
    "Malformed persisted entries are repaired (defaulted) when possible and dropped when irrecoverable, so the app never crashes on bad stored data.",
    "The idea does not request search/sort or due dates, so those are intentionally omitted."
  ],
